# DCLF's Lighting draws without Light Limit Fix (CS_DISABLE_FEATURES): each draw picks its point lights from DCLF's frame table
# (dclf-architecture.md, "Point lights without Light Limit Fix"). Whiterun at night, then Dragonsreach (braziers, torches) with two
# shadowless green lights (DefaultGreen01NS) placed at the player; each view shot with DCLF, then again with DCLF off (dclf:feature=0),
# whose draws are the engine's with its own per-object lights.
# Compare each shot with its -off twin: light pools on floors, walls, tables and NPCs near torches and braziers, and the green light
# around the player, must match. Before the table DCLF's objects took no point light at all (sun and ambient only).
# Log: "Feature 'LightLimitFix' is disabled at boot by CS_DISABLE_FEATURES", no line naming LIGHT_LIMIT_FIX in the SPIR-V builds'
# defines, no [E] but EFFECTS11's, no "Render graph disabled" or "Forced off".
CS_DISABLE_FEATURES=LightLimitFix
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=300:set timescale to 0;301:set gamehour to 22;400:coc Whiterun;1300:set timescale to 0;1310:set gamehour to 22;1320:tai;1500:dclf:shot=whiterun;1520:dclf:feature=0;1800:dclf:shot=whiterun-off;1820:dclf:feature=1;1900:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;2700:tai;2710:player.placeatme f7cc2 2;3000:dclf:shot=dragonsreach;3020:dclf:feature=0;3300:dclf:shot=dragonsreach-off;3320:dclf:feature=1
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=3500
